# QA CI/CD Automation

![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.13-blue)
![Pytest](https://img.shields.io/badge/Pytest-9.1.1-green)
![GitHub Actions](https://img.shields.io/badge/GitHub%20Actions-CI%2FCD-black)

A QA automation project demonstrating automated testing with **Python and Pytest**, integrated with a **GitHub Actions CI/CD pipeline**.

## 📌 Project Overview

This project demonstrates how automated tests can be integrated into a CI/CD workflow.

Whenever code is pushed to the `main` branch or a pull request is created, GitHub Actions automatically:

1. Checks out the repository
2. Sets up Python
3. Installs the required dependencies
4. Runs the Pytest test suite
5. Reports the test results

This helps ensure that automated tests are executed consistently whenever the code changes.

---

