## 🧪 Test Cases

The project currently contains three automated test cases:

| Test Case               | Purpose                            |
| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| `test_login_validation` | Validates login-related test logic |
| `test_product_price`    | Validates product price            |
| `test_cart_item_count`  | Validates cart item count          |

### Local Test Result

All three tests currently pass successfully.

```text
3 passed in 0.02s
```

---

## ⚙️ Running the Tests Locally

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/QA-CI-CD-Automation.git
```

### 2. Navigate to the project

```bash
cd QA-CI-CD-Automation
```

### 3. Create a virtual environment

```bash
python -m venv venv
```

### 4. Activate the virtual environment

For Windows PowerShell:

```powershell
venv\Scripts\activate
```

### 5. Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 6. Run the tests

```bash
pytest -v
```

Expected result:

```text
3 passed
```

---

## 🔄 CI/CD Pipeline

This project uses **GitHub Actions** for continuous integration.

The workflow file is located at:

```text
.github/workflows/tests.yml
```

### Pipeline Flow

```text
Code Push / Pull Request
          ↓
    GitHub Actions
          ↓
   Checkout Repository
          ↓
     Setup Python
          ↓
 Install Dependencies
          ↓
      Run Pytest
          ↓
    Test Results
```

### Workflow Triggers

The CI pipeline runs when:

* Code is pushed to the `main` branch
* A pull request is created or updated against the `main` branch

---

## 📄 GitHub Actions Workflow

The GitHub Actions workflow:

* Uses an Ubuntu environment
* Sets up Python 3.13
* Installs dependencies from `requirements.txt`
* Executes the Pytest test suite

The main test command used by the workflow is:

```bash
pytest -v
```

